  "title": "Al-Azhar Mosque",
  "summary": "Al-Azhar Mosque in Cairo was established in 970 by Jawhar the Sicilian, a general of the Fatimid caliph al-Mu'izz, as the official mosque of the new regime. EBSCO dates its completion to 972, its first class to 975, and an official school with scholars teaching jurisprudence to 988-989. Encyclopedia.com calls al-Azhar's university the world's oldest school of higher learning in continuous operation.",
